==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|p|a}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*pardas}}, borrowed from {{bor|fi|gem-pro|*bardaz||edge}}, compare {{cog|non|barð||brim, verge}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|parras}}, {{cog|liv|pārdaz}}, {{cog|lud|pardaz}}. 

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# A [[brink]], [[verge]] or [[edge]].
#: ''tuhon '''partaalla'''''
#:: on the brink of destruction
#: ''olla haudan '''partaalla'''''
#:: to have one foot in the grave
#:: to be [[on one's last legs]]
# When used to express being very close to do something, [[about]].
#: ''Hän oli itkun '''partaalla'''.''
#:: She was about to cry.
# {{lb|fi|nautical}} A [[rail]].

====Usage notes====
In the sense "brink, verge, edge" rarely used except in [[adessive]] (on), [[ablative]] (from) or [[allative]] (onto).

